Description: properties: Add depth to display and inset to shadow
 .
 depth is where an element is shown in depth on a stereo output, relative
 to what it lies on, as a fraction of the user's range: -1.0 is the sunk
 limit, 0.0 the plane it lies on and 1.0 the popped limit. It moves the
 whole element, text included, and never changes the layout; a 2D output
 shows the element as it is without depth.
 .
 inset marks a shadow cast inside the element, CSS Backgrounds 3's inset
 keyword, which may come first or last in box-shadow. Without depth, an
 outer shadow will raise an element and an inset one sink it.
 .
 The syntax also takes <integer> because the parser does not match
 integers against <number>.
