 The opacity of the element.
 
 
+\section3 depth (sunk | screen | popped | <percentage> | <number> | <integer>)
+
+The depth of the element on a stereo output, relative to what the element lies on:
+how far the element and everything it contains, its text included, are shown in
+front of it or behind it. \c{sunk} is the sunk limit, \c{screen} the plane of what
+the element lies on and \c{popped} the popped limit; a percentage or a number from
+-100% (-1.0) to 100% (1.0) is a fraction of the limit on its side. The limits are the
+user's settings. A value outside that range is ignored.
+
+When a style declares no depth for an element, the element's shadow gives it one:
+an outer shadow raises the element by half of the popped limit, an inset shadow
+sinks it to the sunk limit, and an element without a shadow lies on what it is drawn
+on. The depth never changes the layout, and a 2D output shows the element exactly as
+it is without depth.
+
+
+
 
 \section2 layout
 
@@ -775,11 +792,12 @@ The radius of the corner.
 
 These properties describe an element's shadow.
 
-\section3 box-shadow (none | (<length> <length> <length> <length> <color>))
+\section3 box-shadow (none | (<length> <length> <length> <length> <color> inset) | (inset <length> <length> <length> <length> <color>) | (<length> <length> <length> <length> <color>))
 
 A shorthand to set the shadow of an element to a box-shaped shadow. If set to none,
 the shadow will explicitly be disabled. Otherwise, the parameters are X offset, Y offset,
-size, blur and finally color.
+blur, size and finally color, with an optional \c{inset} keyword first or last for a
+shadow inside the element.
 
 
 
